The person's per-file choice for a video (the input packing chosen by hand, Not 3D, the swap of the eyes) is read
from the stereo layer's per-file store, where Dolphin's "3D Input Format" menu keeps it, and no longer from the file
attribute user.stereo-policy.swap-eyes (ORDER 512 and 551; Daniel, 2026-10-23: "never touch the user file").

An anaglyph the person chose by hand for a video gives a thumbnail with both views, taken out of the colours.
Views that come one after the other in time (a frame sequence, both views in one block) are not in one frame: the
thumbnail shows the view its frame holds, and the menu says so.

Built against libstereo-layer-dev 1.18.0, and the build stops with CMake's message when the layer is older
(CMAKE_REQUIRE_FIND_PACKAGE_StereoLayer): before, an older layer gave a thumbnailer without stereo and no error.
